# Tasks

Hand-authored intent only. Status never lives here — it lives in
`.crew/state.json`, and `crew status` is how you read it.

The first mate writes tasks into this file after you confirm an interview.
You can write them yourself; the shape is:

```markdown
## task: <kebab-case-id>
- depends_on: none
- paths: {{.PathsExample}}
- brief: >
    What to build, and any constraint that matters.
    Say explicitly what not to touch.
- acceptance_criteria:
    - check: "{{.CheckExample}}"
      description: A plain statement of the behaviour.
    - judged: true
      description: Something that genuinely needs a reading.
```

`paths` is a mutual-exclusion declaration: two tasks with overlapping paths
cannot be in flight at once. Each criterion is either a check command or
`judged: true` — never both, never neither.
